.venv
__pycache__
uploads/
myenv/
venv/
deploy/
.env
# The whole git history was being COPYed into the production image: every past revision, every
# branch name, every author email, in an artifact that only needs the working tree. It also made
# the image non-deterministic for no benefit, and -- found the hard way -- it made `.git` present
# inside the runtime, so a test discriminating "checkout" from "shipped image" got the wrong
# answer. Nothing in the build or the runtime reads git: the build revision arrives as a build
# ARG.
.git/
.github/
